<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-314] pyspark is not responding for Python 3</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-314</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Tried to run pyspark with Python 3.4.3 as below.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;%pyspark&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;import sys&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;print(sys.version_info)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;pyspark is not responding   File &quot;/tmp/zeppelin_pyspark.py&quot;, line 55&lt;br/&gt;
    print gateway.jvm.org.apache.zeppelin.spark.ZeppelinContext.showDF(self.z, obj._jdf)&lt;br/&gt;
                ^&lt;br/&gt;
SyntaxError: invalid syntax&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It seems is not Python3 syntax.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;Ubuntu 15.04&lt;br/&gt;
from apt: OpenJDK 1.7.0_85, Maven 3.3.3, Python 3.4.3&lt;br/&gt;
built from site files: Scala 2.10.6, Spark 1.5.2, Zeppelin from git (commit 0665cef059b)&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
