                            <comment id="15081399" author="paulochf" created="Mon, 4 Jan 2016 17:19:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hey!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issues was resolved, but after that it came back again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;%pyspark&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;import sys&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;print(sys.version_info)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;pyspark is not responding   File &quot;/tmp/zeppelin_pyspark.py&quot;, line 150&lt;br/&gt;
    print &quot;&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
           ^&lt;br/&gt;
SyntaxError: Missing parentheses in call to &apos;print&apos;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would like to point out that there&apos;s some lines I would be careful. Following some conversion guide (i.e. &lt;a href=&quot;http://python-future.org/compatible_idioms.html):&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://python-future.org/compatible_idioms.html):&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;86  : &lt;tt&gt;tuples = map(lambda items: self.__tupleToScalaTuple2(items), options)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
152: &lt;tt&gt;print json.dumps(filter(lambda x : not re.match(&quot;^__.*&quot;, x), list(completionList)))&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;map()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;filter()&lt;/tt&gt; now return iterators. To get the list, do&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;list(map(...))&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;list(filter(...))&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;114: &lt;tt&gt;for completionItem in list(globals().iterkeys()):&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;.iterkeys()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;.itervalues()&lt;/tt&gt; are now &lt;tt&gt;.keys()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;.values()&lt;/tt&gt;, giving iterators. If the list is desired, do the above.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
